{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/workingwithquantity"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/WorkingWithQuantity","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/StoringAndEncodingQuantities","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitsByDimension","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create, convert, compare, compute with, and format "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" values in your app.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity"},{"type":"text","text":" is the type you’ll reach for most often. It works the way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Foundation’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Measurement"},{"type":"text","text":" does, but with compile-time dimension checking: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"quantity always knows its unit, and its unit knows its "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This article covers everything you can do with a quantity, grouped the same way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Apple documents its own value types."}]},{"anchor":"Create-a-Quantity","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Create a Quantity"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a quantity with a value and a unit using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/init(value:unit:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Math","","\/\/ Distance","let jumpLength = Quantity(value: 8.95, unit: Units.meter)","","\/\/ Money — currency units place their symbol before the value ($8.95)","let price = Quantity(value: 8.95, unit: Units.usd)","","\/\/ Temperature — offset units like Celsius convert correctly","let bodyTemp = Quantity(value: 37.0, unit: Units.celsius)"]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The value is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decimal"},{"type":"text","text":", so you can pass integer and decimal literals"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directly: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Quantity(value: 42, unit: Units.kilometer)"},{"type":"text","text":". Decimal arithmetic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps base-10 values exact—"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.1 + 0.2"},{"type":"text","text":" really is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.3"},{"type":"text","text":"—which matters for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"money, scientific constants, and repeated conversions."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note"},{"anchor":"Convert-Between-Units","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Convert Between Units"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/converted(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to convert to another unit of the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension. The framework converts through the unit’s base unit, so arbitrary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chains like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nanometer → kilometer"},{"type":"text","text":" just work:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let chipFeature = Quantity(value: 5.0, unit: Units.nanometer)","let inMeters = chipFeature.converted(to: Units.meter)","print(inMeters.value) \/\/ 5e-09","","let marathon = Quantity(value: 42.195, unit: Units.kilometer)","print(marathon.converted(to: Units.mile).value) \/\/ 26.218...","","let paycheck = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: Units.eur)","print(paycheck.converted(to: Units.usd).value) \/\/ 108.0"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because conversions require matching dimensions, converting a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"length"},{"type":"text","text":" to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t compile (or traps at runtime if the units are fully dynamic)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety","isActive":true},{"text":" for details.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Compare Quantities","anchor":"Compare-Quantities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Quantities of the same unit type compare by their values with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":". To compare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"quantities expressed in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"different"}]},{"type":"text","text":" units of the same dimension—or to allow a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"small tolerance—use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/isEquivalent(to:tolerance:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let oneMile = Quantity(value: 1.0, unit: Units.mile)","let oneKm    = Quantity(value: 1.0, unit: Units.kilometer)","","oneMile.isEquivalent(to: Quantity(value: 1609.344, unit: Units.meter)) \/\/ true","oneMile.isEquivalent(to: oneKm)                                        \/\/ false"]},{"anchor":"Add-and-Subtract-Quantities","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Add and Subtract Quantities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can add and subtract quantities of the same dimension even when their units"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"differ. The result keeps the left-hand side’s unit; the right-hand side is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converted automatically:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let dish = Quantity(value: 1.5, unit: Units.kilogram)","let spice = Quantity(value: 350.0, unit: Units.gram)","","let total = dish + spice","print(total) \/\/ 1.85 kg"]},{"anchor":"Multiply-and-Divide-Quantities","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Multiply and Divide Quantities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Multiplying or dividing two quantities combines their dimensions. Multiplication"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produces a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompositeUnit"},{"type":"text","text":"; division produces a typed "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/RatioUnit"},{"text":" that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remembers which operand was on top. The framework adjusts both the numeric value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the coefficient so results stay physically correct:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let area = Quantity(value: 3.0, unit: Units.meter) * Quantity(value: 2.0, unit: Units.meter)","print(area.value)          \/\/ 6.0","print(area.unit.symbol)    \/\/ \"(m*m)\"","print(area.unit.dimension) \/\/ area","","let speed = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: Units.meter) \/ Quantity(value: 5.0, unit: Units.second)","print(speed.value)          \/\/ 20.0","print(speed.unit.symbol)    \/\/ \"(m\/s)\"","print(speed.unit.dimension) \/\/ speed"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also multiply and divide a quantity by a plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decimal"},{"text":" scalar, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps the same unit:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let doubling = Quantity(value: 5.0, unit: Units.meter) * 2","print(doubling) \/\/ 10.00 m"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For common derived dimensions, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"text":" produces cleaner units. For example,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiplying a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/power","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" by a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/time","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" yields an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"energy unit with the conventional symbol ordering:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let power   = Quantity(value: 2.0, unit: Units.kilowatt)","let runTime = Quantity(value: 3.0, unit: Units.hour)","let energy  = power * runTime    \/\/ 6 kWh, dimension = energy"]},{"anchor":"Typed-Ratio-Units","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Typed Ratio Units"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sometimes you don’t just want a measurement — you want the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"type system"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remember which side of a ratio something is on. A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompositeUnit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(usd\/kg)"},{"text":" erases that detail (its compile-time dimension is always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unknown"},{"text":"), so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"USD per kilogram"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kilogram per USD"},{"text":" become the same type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/RatioUnit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" keeps the numerator and denominator as two distinct generic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameters, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"USD \/ kg"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"different type"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kg \/ USD"},{"text":". Build one with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"``MathUnit\/per(_:)`, the initializer, or just divide two quantities:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let price = Units.usd.per(Units.kilogram)            \/\/ (usd\/kg)","let hoursPerDollar = Units.hour.per(Units.usd)       \/\/ (h\/$)","let fromDivision = Quantity(value: 40, unit: Units.usd)","                \/ Quantity(value: 5, unit: Units.Weight.pound)  \/\/ ($\/lbf)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the ordering is baked into the type, a generic function can require a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specific arrangement. Here the denominator must ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"be"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" a currency unit:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func denominatedInCurrency<Num: MathUnit>(","    _ value: Quantity<RatioUnit<Num, NamedUnit<MathDimension.currency>>>",") -> Bool { ... }","","denominatedInCurrency(Quantity(value: 2, unit: Units.hour.per(Units.usd)))  \/\/ ✔","denominatedInCurrency(Quantity(value: 20, unit: Units.usd.per(Units.hour))) \/\/ ✘ won't compile"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Multiplying a ratio by its denominator cancels the denominator and returns the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"numerator: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"price * amount → money"},{"text":". Both operand orders work, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"math always runs through base units so coefficients stay exact:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let cost = Quantity(value: 3.5, unit: Units.usd.per(Units.kilogram))","         * Quantity(value: 2, unit: Units.kilogram)   \/\/ $7.00"]},{"anchor":"Format-Quantities","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Format Quantities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"text":", so it prints a formatted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string automatically. Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/formatted(decimalPlaces:includeSpace:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to control the decimal places and spacing. Currency symbols are placed before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the value by default; most other symbols follow it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let tenDollars = Quantity(value: 10.1234, unit: Units.usd)","print(tenDollars.formatted())                 \/\/ \"$10.12\"","print(tenDollars.formatted(decimalPlaces: 3)) \/\/ \"$10.123\"","","let fiveMeters = Quantity(value: 5.5, unit: Units.meter)","print(fiveMeters.formatted())                 \/\/ \"5.50 m\"","print(fiveMeters.formatted(includeSpace: false)) \/\/ \"5.50m\"","","let percent = Quantity(value: 75.5, unit: Units.percent)","print(percent.formatted())                    \/\/ \"75.50%\""]},{"anchor":"Store-Mixed-Dimensions-with-AnyQuantity","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Store Mixed Dimensions with `AnyQuantity`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"‘s unit type is part of its Swift type, so a single array cannot","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hold a length, a mass, and a count of tea bags. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/AnyQuantity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" erases that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile-time dimension while preserving the unit’s runtime behavior:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let ingredients: [AnyQuantity] = [","    AnyQuantity(value: 250, unit: Units.gram),","    AnyQuantity(value: 8, unit: Units.fluidOunce),","    AnyQuantity(value: 2, unit: CountUnit(item: \"tea bag\")),","]","","for ingredient in ingredients {","    print(ingredient.simplified()) \/\/ 250.00 g, 8.00 fl oz, 2.00 tea bag","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnyQuantity"},{"type":"text","text":" converts (returning either a typed "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or another erased"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"quantity), simplifies, formats, compares for physical equivalence, and supports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/"},{"type":"text","text":" operators as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","isActive":true},{"text":". Compatibility is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"checked at runtime, so adding a mass to a length traps instead of compiling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"silently.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An erased quantity is also "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":". Its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/AnyMathUnit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" records the symbol,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension, converter, symbol position, identity, and conversion family, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON round trip restores a fully functional unit:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let data = try JSONEncoder().encode(ingredients)","let decoded = try JSONDecoder().decode([AnyQuantity].self, from: data)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To restore a statically typed value when you know the unit type, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/AnyQuantity\/typed(as:)","type":"reference"},{"text":". You can also erase any typed quantity with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/anyQuantity","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For units alone, use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/AnyMathUnit","type":"reference"},{"text":"; for runtime dimensions, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/AnyDimension","type":"reference"},{"text":". Both are ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"What’s Next?","anchor":"Whats-Next","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Browse the ready-made units in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"type":"text","text":" or define your own named units with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/NamedUnit"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build composite units dynamically by combining units with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operators defined for "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathUnit"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to define units for your own domain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety","type":"reference"},{"text":" to make dimension correctness a compile-time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"guarantee.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"role":"article","title":"Working with Quantity","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"references":{"doc://Math/documentation/Math/AnyDimension":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier